{"name":"Elusive Dawn","hex":"#d5bfad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elusive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Evading capture, comprehension or remembrance.","Difficult to make precise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elusive"},{"term":"dawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To begin to brighten with daylight.","To start to appear or become obvious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The morning twilight period immediately before sunrise.","The rising of the sun."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elusive","blocks":[{"text":"\"Elusive\" was the first single for British singer-songwriter Scott Matthews and was released on 18 September 2006. The single received much airplay from BBC Radio DJs Jo Whiley, Dermot O'Leary and Zane Lowe between 7 and 10 August. Lowe also played \"Elusive\" once each night as his chosen Single of the Week. Matthews also visited the station to perform \"Elusive\" and other songs from the album in May and August 2006. In May 2007, he won the Ivor Novello Award for \"Best Song Musically and Lyrically\" which saw \"Elusive\" beat strong competition from the likes of the Arctic Monkeys."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elusive"},{"title":"Dawn","blocks":[{"text":"Dawn is the time that marks the beginning of twilight before sunrise. It is recognized by the appearance of indirect daylight being scattered in Earth's atmosphere, when the centre of the Sun's disc has reached 18° below the observer's horizon. This morning twilight period will last until sunrise, when direct daylight outshines the diffused light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Desert_Dawn.jpg/330px-Desert_Dawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/500px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/1280px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/500px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dawn at La Silla Observatory, Chile[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg/500px-Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg/1280px-Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg/500px-Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dawn over Serra dos Órgãos National Park, Rio de Janeiro state, Brazil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.jpg/60px-L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.jpg/120px-L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.jpg/60px-L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.